# hexagonrpcd — the FastRPC file server for Qualcomm Hexagon DSPs, built FROM SOURCE via a
# retroforge-owned PKGBUILD (packages/hexagonrpcd/PKGBUILD). The ADSP's sensors PD on the Air X
# reads its registry and configs through it. Not in the holo snapshot.
#
# After adding or bumping this: `make relock` (the package must land in rootfs/manifest.lock; it is
# listed in PKGS in rootfs/customize-base.sh).
#
# Patch, ours:
#   0001  the ADSP units no longer conflict with suspend.target, which stopped them for good.
name: hexagonrpcd
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
patches: 0001-data-keep-the-ADSP-servers-running-across-suspend.patch
pkgrel_suffix: 1
